# ==========================================================================
# Launder WM — .build-docs/TECH_PLAN.md §11.3 (.dockerignore) and §3 (layout).
# What must never enter git, and why.
# ==========================================================================

# Secrets. .env holds OPENAI_API_KEY / HF_TOKEN. The
# generic template above already ignores `.env`; these are the siblings.
.env
.env.*
!.env.example

# Build INPUTS for the tokenizer packer, not build outputs. The 33 MB
# google/gemma-3-4b-it tokenizer.json is what `forge tok pack` reads; the
# 1,192,944-byte packed blob in data/assets/ is what ships and IS committed.
data/build/

# The fat intermediate that triage reads: token_ids, g_values_b64,
# scored_mask_b64, word_spans, token_char_spans, prefix_z, reject_reasons.
# Hundreds of MB per 400-candidate run.
data/candidates/

# forge doctor output + seeds + versions, per generation run. Provenance, but
# machine-local and regenerated every session.
data/runs/

# Model weights, ever, by accident. 8.64 GB for gemma-3-4b-it.
*.pt
*.pth
*.ckpt
*.gguf
*.safetensors

# Local artifacts
web/node_modules/
web/dist/
web/test-results/
web/playwright-report/
node_modules/
reports/
exports/
scratch/
*.sqlite3
# WAL and shared-memory siblings. `*.sqlite3` did not cover them, so booting
# the dev server once left `launder-dev.sqlite3-wal` and `launder-dev.sqlite3-shm`
# untracked-and-not-ignored at the repo root, and the first `git add -A`
# committed them. The dev DB runs in WAL mode deliberately (§9.6).
*.sqlite3-wal
*.sqlite3-shm
*.db-wal
*.db-shm

# NOT ignored, stated so nobody "cleans" them up:
#   uv.lock                              one lock for all three members
#   data/assets/**                       key material + the packed blob
#   data/golden/**                       the parity gate, read by pytest AND vitest
#   data/config/**                       every tunable in the modularity contract
#   data/passages/*.author.json          repo only, but COMMITTED — it is the
#                                        answer key and the provenance record;
#                                        it is excluded from the IMAGE, not git
#   tools/reference/**                   provenance for the ports

# Answer keys for the 15 levels, generated by .solutions/solve.py for
# manual testing. Never committed: the whole game is that you work the
# solution out, and a copy-pasteable one in the repo ends it.
.solutions/
